  "readmeFile": "PACKAGE.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Streaming breadth and correctness. The streamability analysis is now compositional (posture/sweep over the expression tree) rather than a fixed set of recognized shapes, so many more streamable constructs are accepted and executed as true streaming instead of falling back to whole-input buffering or empty output. Newly streamed correctly: xsl:apply-templates over a downward select (dispatching the matched template body per node, with tunnel and non-tunnel parameters); general comparisons over a per-item attribute-arithmetic tail such as (path/(@value*2)) = n; the absorbing/windowing functions head, tail, subsequence, remove, insert-before and sum's empty default; xsl:message and xsl:assert as grounding sinks; namespace-wildcard (*:name) selects; value-of / xsl:attribute atomization and separators over a streamed sequence; ancestor/climbing populations; and xsl:iterate over a grounded atomic crawl. Also corrects xsl:attribute simple-content node merging on the non-streaming path. Requires PhoenixmlDb.Core 1.2.0 and PhoenixmlDb.XQuery 1.5.2. No API changes. See RELEASES.md for full notes.",
